Task: Fields the engine uses
Mark each kept tag field with whether the engine reads what the importer fills from it

The spec's third mark: a field the importer keeps is used when the
engine reads it. The importer's readers now record the label of each
read; the census traces a label through the call it is passed to, to
the field or local that call fills, and looks for that name read
through a '.' in the engine's crates (not the importer, the census or
the CLI, and not their test modules).

Of 2811 kept fields, 2144 are used, 516 unused (declared in content
and read nowhere, e.g. the biped's slope and landing fields, checked by
hand) and 151 untraced (labels passed through helpers the trace cannot
follow). The match is by name, so a name two types share can overstate
'used'.

Checked: the workspace's 1273 tests, clippy, census --check.
